<title>USA: Geberit Int'l sells 157.5 mln marks in junk bonds.</title>
<headline>Geberit Int'l sells 157.5 mln marks in junk bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following mark-denominated 144a global high-yield bond issue from Geberit International SA was priced on Thursday via lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, market sources said.</p>
<p>Geberit is a unit of Geberit Beteilingungs AG, a Swiss company that was taken over in leveraged buyout by London-based Doughty Hanson.</p>
<p>The company manufactures sanitary plumbing products.</p>
<p>BORROWER GEBERIT INTERNATIONAL SA</p>
<p>AMT 157.5 MLN MARKS (APPROXIMATELY $92 MLN)</p>
<p>COUPON 10.125 PCT</p>
<p>MATURITY 4/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE GLOBAL SENIOR SUBORDINATED NOTES</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE 100</p>
<p>YIELD 10.125 PCT</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS</p>
<p>SPREAD NA</p>
<p>CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE FOR FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>PAY FREQ SEMI ANNUAL</p>
<p>SETTLEMENT DATE 4/17/97</p>
<p>FULL FEES THREE PERCENT</p>
<p>NOTE: THREE-YEAR EQUITY CALL FOR 35 PERCENT OF THE ISSUE AT</p>
<p>110; THE NOTES WILL BE LISTED IN FRANKFURT</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
